# Slice 296 probe (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM): inside a named Structure's body a head nothing binds there, with a name as its
# tail (`fld: a`), is a nested named Structure with that written content; T's own field stays as written.  Entry 7; a
# wrong value leaves as the exit code.
T:
    int: a 1
    fld: a
end: T
int: code 7
call: T\fld
if: T\a != 1
    code: T\a
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
